{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZNbaMbW3xCzfBJvtuPE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate, and it passes the admission self-check (`OK`). The files are in `experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_2/`.\n\n**Hypothesis (`personal_switch_rate_prototype`):** each person has their own idea of how often a random coin switches between heads and tails. They judge a sequence as random to the extent its switch rate is close to that personal ideal. Because people's ideals differ, the same pair can be judged in opposite directions by different participants.\n\n**Why this one:** the critique's only discrepancy that survived the FDR correction is a gap between participants. People differ in how often they pick the more-alternating sequence far more than the single-population `local_representativeness` model predicts (observed spread 0.217 vs 0.053, q = 0.016). None of the existing models uses the `participant_id` information. The best model does have an alternation target, but it is one value for everyone.\n\n**Model:**\n- Each participant's ideal switch rate is drawn from a shared population distribution.\n- Randomness is the negative squared distance between a sequence's switch rate and that ideal.\n- The choice is a logistic function of the difference between the two sequences, with one shared sensitivity.\n\n**Smoke-fit result:** ELPD-LOO was about −1009, against −1398 for the current best. That was only a 1-chain, 100-draw fit, so treat the number as a rough sign, not a result.\n\n**Caveats that may cost it at admission:**\n- **LOO reliability:** the smoke fit flagged 4.6% of trials with high Pareto-k, above the 1% tolerance. If the full fit stays over that, the model can't be exported as the winner and is the first to be retired by the live-set cap.\n- **Not checked yet:** convergence (R-hat can't be computed from one chain) and novelty against the other models. For the novelty check, admission averages its predictions over the training participants.\n- **Screened out of designs:** because it uses `participant_id`, it will be recorded in `screened_out.json` and left out of later stimulus designs.\n- **Extra parameters:** it reserves 512 per-participant slots so that participant IDs from later experiments still fit. Slots with no participant just follow the population prior, but they add some sampling time. The smoke fit took 38 s."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2483,"cache_read_input_tokens":54452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2483,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df8ca9d8-c004-4558-86cc-62bc91e3d4a6","uuid":"088767fc-be04-45a9-bf4f-632fbffc8947","timestamp":"2026-09-30T09:17:52.097Z","request_id":"req_011CfZNbZmcMKs1SXixoBUnz"}
